      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the given ratio of girls to boys, which is 3:2. This means that for every 3 girls, there are 2 boys in the class. \n\nFirst, let's find the total number of parts in the ratio:\n3 parts (girls) + 2 parts (boys) = 5 parts\n\nNow, we know that there are a total of 45 students in the class. We can set up an equation to find the value of one part:\n1 part = 45 students ÷ 5 parts = 9 students per part\n\nSince there are 3 parts representing girls, we can find the number of girls by multiplying the value of one part by the number of parts:\nNumber of girls = 3 parts × 9 students per part = 27 students\n\nSo, there are 27 girls in Ms. Snow's math class.",
